Before I was born, the story goes, Grandpa and
Grandma were duck hunting. They each shoot, and hit
their target. Grandpa politely lets Grandma send the
black Labrador, Jet, after her kill. The dog comes
swimming back with a duck in his mouth, and Grandpa
goes to send Jet after _his_ kill. "Not so fast",
says Grandma. "First, let him bring back my _other_
duck." Seems Grandma liked to save shotgun shells by
waiting until the ducks were lined up, and then
shooting two at once.

Two generations later, I couldn't hit a bird on the
wing by firing a shotgun if it meant the difference
between starving to death, and living a long happy
life.  I'd be better off throwing the shotgun at the
bird, to knock it down that way.




